meta {
  name: S22 unflag and quota
  seq: 20
}

docs {
  Story S22, TICK-740 (kit TICK-754, docs/acceptance/S22/README.md): a tenant admin removes the `x-nava-filterable` flag from a field and its index is cleaned up (ADR-006 D11); flagging it again while the removal runs answers 409 `field_index_busy` (D8); a sixth flagged field on a type answers 422 `index_quota_exceeded` until the operator raises the tenant's per-type limit to 10 (D12); the seed types' filters run through the index only (D6). Needs the stack docs/acceptance/S22/tools/run-kit.sh prepares: tenant A's type `s22_asset` with `s22_code` (string, not flagged) and 20,000 records, 1,000 per value K00..K19. Story users: `admin@tenant-a` publishes, `agent@tenant-a` is Alice, `operator` raises the limit. AC3 (S22.4-S22.6): the seed types. AC1 (S22.7-S22.14): unflag, 400 at once, 409 while removing, flag again after. AC4 (S22.11, S22.14, verify.sql): records written during the removal leave no orphan side rows. AC2 (S22.15-S22.24): the quota, the refused limit changes and the audited operator raise. Runs once per prepared stack.
}
